4:["$","main",null,{"className":"blog-page","children":[["$","$Le",null,{}],["$","article",null,{"className":"blog-article","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"shell blog-article-shell","children":[["$","$Lf",null,{"className":"blog-back-link","href":"/blog","children":[["$","$L10",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7","key":"1l729n"}],["path",{"d":"M19 12H5","key":"x3x0zl"}]],"className":"lucide-arrow-left","size":16}]," All guides"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"blog-tag","children":["Destinations"," · ","One Window archive"]}],["$","h1",null,{"children":"Is studying abroad in UK worth it for Indian students?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"blog-article-intro","children":"As Indian students, we’re often met with two questions that everyone seems to be dying to know the answer to – 1) why should I study abroad? 2) which country should I choose to study in? While these are both valid and important questions, it’s worth remembering that no matter where you choose to study abroad, there will always be advantages and disadvantages. So before you embark on your international student journey, keep these things in mind as you decide whether or not study abroad in UK is worth it for Indian students. Study Abroad India offers quality degree programs and a wide range of options to choose from. There are also plenty of opportunities to work after graduation. But is studying abroad in UK really worth it, or should you consider staying back in India instead? Here’s what you need to know"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-article-body","children":[["$","section","The guide",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"The guide"}],[["$","p","Study Abroad in U.K.",{"children":"Study Abroad in U.K."}],["$","p","The Study abroad in UK campaign was a joint initiative by British Council, Department of Education and Science and Higher Education Funding Council for England. The aim of these three bodies was to urge potential overseas students to see what U.K has to offer when it comes to top class higher education. Britain offers world class universities that provide challenging courses and excellent learning environments. It is no wonder why so many people look at Britain as their first choice when it comes to study abroad destinations. Students who have studied in U.K have time and again praised its educational system; they have also had nothing but good things to say about campus life too! Studying in Britain is certainly one of those ‘must do’ kind of things if you’re looking to pursue an international degree program today!",{"children":"The Study abroad in UK campaign was a joint initiative by British Council, Department of Education and Science and Higher Education Funding Council for England. The aim of these three bodies was to urge potential overseas students to see what U.K has to offer when it comes to top class higher education. Britain offers world class universities that provide challenging courses and excellent learning environments. It is no wonder why so many people look at Britain as their first choice when it comes to study abroad destinations. Students who have studied in U.K have time and again praised its educational system; they have also had nothing but good things to say about campus life too! Studying in Britain is certainly one of those ‘must do’ kind of things if you’re looking to pursue an international degree program today!"}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}],["$","section","Cost of Studying Abroad in UK",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Cost of Studying Abroad in UK"}],["$L11","$L12","$L13","$L14","$L15"],"$L16"]}],"$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c"]}],"$L1d"]}]}],"$L1e"]}]
:HL["/Logos/OW%20web%20desktop%20logos%20(200%20x%2040%20px)/OW%20White%20Logo%20desktop.png","image"]
11:["$","p","Cost is a major consideration when studying abroad. Expenses such as tuition fees, living costs, visa application fees and travel expenses must be planned and budgeted before you leave. The cost of studying varies according to where you want to study, so it’s essential to do your research first. Compare tuition fees at institutions of your choice and find out what kind of financial aid is available. The average annual fee at top universities is around £9000-£12000 (£2000-3000 per year). However, some may ask for higher tuition fees. Check whether they offer any",{"children":"Cost is a major consideration when studying abroad. Expenses such as tuition fees, living costs, visa application fees and travel expenses must be planned and budgeted before you leave. The cost of studying varies according to where you want to study, so it’s essential to do your research first. Compare tuition fees at institutions of your choice and find out what kind of financial aid is available. The average annual fee at top universities is around £9000-£12000 (£2000-3000 per year). However, some may ask for higher tuition fees. Check whether they offer any"}]
12:["$","p","scholarships",{"children":"scholarships"}]
13:["$","p","that are open to international students or have an exchange program with any foreign institution. These programs can save up to 50% on your overall costs!",{"children":"that are open to international students or have an exchange program with any foreign institution. These programs can save up to 50% on your overall costs!"}]
14:["$","p","Living Expenses",{"children":"Living Expenses"}]
15:["$","p","Most of us don’t realize just how much a life overseas can cost. While tuition may be comparable, or even lower than studying at home, and overall quality may be better, there are many other costs you’ll want to plan for – especially if you want to stay living overseas after graduation. There will be extra costs added to your living expenses that come with studying abroad. Just because they weren’t included in your education doesn’t mean they won’t be part of it. Before you take any more loans out, sit down and crunch some numbers with",{"children":"Most of us don’t realize just how much a life overseas can cost. While tuition may be comparable, or even lower than studying at home, and overall quality may be better, there are many other costs you’ll want to plan for – especially if you want to stay living overseas after graduation. There will be extra costs added to your living expenses that come with studying abroad. Just because they weren’t included in your education doesn’t mean they won’t be part of it. Before you take any more loans out, sit down and crunch some numbers with"}]
